==Esperanto==
===Etymology===
From the noun ''[[flugo]]''

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈfluɡi/|lang=eo}}
* {{hyphenation|flu|gi}}

===Verb===
{{eo-verb|flug}}

# to [[fly]]
#: Ĉiu aŭtuno, anseroj suden '''flugas'''.
#: ''Each fall, geese '''fly''' south.''

====Conjugation====
{{eo-conj|flug}}

====Related terms====
* '''[[ekflugi]]''': to [[take flight]], to [[take off]] (leave the ground)
* '''[[ĉirkaŭflugi]]''': to fly in [[circle]]s, to fly around
* '''[[flugaparato]]''': [[aircraft]], [[airplane]], [[flying machine]]
* '''[[flugarmeisto]]''': [[airman]], [[flyboy]] (both senses limited to members of a national air force)
* '''[[flugarmeo]]''': [[air force]]
* '''[[flugdisko]]''': [[Frisbee]]
* '''[[flughaveno]]''': [[airport]]
* '''[[flugokompanio]]''': [[flight crew]]
* '''[[flugludilo]]''': [[kite]]
* '''[[flugilo]]''': [[wing]]
* '''[[flugmaŝino]]''': [[airplane]], [[aircraft]], [[flying machine]]
* '''[[flugo]]''': [[flight]]
* '''[[fluglino]]''': [[airline]]
* '''[[flugopendi]]''': [[hover]]
* '''[[flugpilkado]]''': [[volleyball]] (the game)
* '''[[flugpilko]]''': volleyball (the ball itself)
* '''[[forflugi]]''': to fly away
* '''[[preterflugi]]''': to fly past

